WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:03.040
The Ethics Committee is&nbsp;
one of the SCP Foundation's&nbsp;

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:05.840
most important and overlooked divisions.

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:11.120
The small, secretive group keeps a close eye
on the Foundation to ensure that all decisions

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:16.960
made and all actions taken are for the betterment
of humanity, and not just in service of needless

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:18.720
sadism and cruelty.

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:23.600
The Ethics Committee consists of a small group
of people in comparison to the gargantuan

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:25.600
that is the Foundation as a whole.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:29.440
It’s only natural that every so often something
slips under their radar.

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:34.080
And when it does, it usually results in complete
and utter disaster.

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:40.560
In the case of SCP-4051, that something is
a male humanoid with a unique ability to open

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:43.280
wormholes to extradimensional spaces.

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:44.960
And in terms of disaster?

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:50.800
Well let’s just say we hope you have a pretty
tight grip on that red SCP Expert coffee mug

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:51.760
of yours.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:58.160
The wormholes that SCP-4051 opens are essentially
spaces filled with infinite copies of a single

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:04.240
item, which SCP-4051 can reach in and pull
out - assuming they're small enough that is.

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:09.440
The Foundation's strict experimentation schedule
has provided a lot of important data on how

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:12.400
SCP-4051's anomaly functions.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:18.400
Controlled testing showed SCP-4051 was able
to manifest small, simple objects like a net,

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:20.480
sugar pills, or drinking water.

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:25.520
But he's also claimed or reported to have
manifested many other things, like aluminim

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:28.160
baseball bats, duct tape, and more.

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:33.760
At one point, SCP-4051 was allowed to use
these abilities to assist with the site, but

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:36.320
the Ethics Committee recently halted this.

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:42.000
Seems like a simple enough anomaly, but with
the Foundation, we all know - it never is.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:45.840
So let's go back - let's start at the very
beginning.

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:52.080
The Foundation first became aware of SCP-4051
when YouTube videos surfaced online of a vigilante

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:55.280
in an American city using wormholes to fight
criminals.

00:01:55.280 --> 00:02:00.080
The videos got over two million views before
the Foundation became aware in August 2012

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:04.320
and stepped in, taking it down and investigating
what had led to it.

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:09.600
A Mobile Task Force was dispatched to retrieve
the individual using the wormholes, and brought

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:13.120
SCP-4051 back to Site-17.

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:17.040
The first interview with SCP-4051 began on
a bad note.

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:22.880
SCP-4051 was handcuffed behind a pane of glass
when Doctor Arthur Roswell began to speak

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:23.520
to him.

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:28.880
Dr. Roswell introduced himself and confirmed
that SCP-4051's name was Rainer Miller.

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:34.480
After being assured of his safety, SCP-4051
calmed down a little and stopped struggling

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:35.600
with the handcuffs.

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:41.760
At Dr. Roswell's request, SCP-4051 began to
explain the details of his anomalous power.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:45.680
He affirmed that he could make small objects
appear out of thin air, and that he tried

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:47.920
to use these abilities to help people.

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:53.040
At first he'd intermittently interrupt carjackings
and robberies, subduing the criminal, but

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:57.840
with a new criminal syndicate moving in, the
crime rate sky-rocketed requiring Rainer to

00:02:57.840 --> 00:02:59.680
patrol much more regularly.

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:04.560
During these acts of heroism, several witnesses
saw Rainer's powers, though he tried to keep

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:05.520
it quiet.

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:09.680
His request for the Foundation to intervene
with the criminal situation was acknowledged

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:14.320
as Rainer volunteered any and all information
he had, stating that he just wanted to help

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:15.440
the Foundation.

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:17.840
Roswell thanked him for his enthusiasm.

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:22.000
It didn't take long for the Foundation to
move to experimenting with Rainer's powers,

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:24.000
as the Foundation often does.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:25.760
At first, they started slow.

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:31.200
Dr. Roswell and his colleague, Dr. Edwards,
asked Rainer to manifest a few small items

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:35.440
- a metal cube, a bottle of bleach, and something
of his choice.

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:39.600
He was able to produce the cube without any
trouble, and the object of his choice wound

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:41.760
up being a framed picture of his mother.

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:46.560
When he tried to take the bleach out, he seemed
upset, but managed to do it.

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:52.160
With the experiment a success, SCP-4051 was
escorted back to his containment chamber.

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:56.720
All the way there, he repeatedly asked how
long this testing phase would take before

00:03:56.720 --> 00:03:58.000
he would be let go.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:00.160
The staff didn't have an answer for him.

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:04.800
In the next test, Rainer was asked by Roswell
and Edwards to produce a copy of War and Peace

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:05.840
and a phone.

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:10.320
Both were produced, but the book was filled
with gibberish, and the phone was entirely

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:10.960
hollow.

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:16.160
The researchers concluded that the anomaly
is based on how well SCP-4051 understands

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:21.200
the object being manifested, and mused about
requesting something that didn't exist.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:25.040
Rainer still asked all of the researchers
how his family was, and whether he would have

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:28.000
any friends at the Foundation between tests.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:31.440
The questions were, once again, ignored by
the staff.

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:35.840
In the third experiment, Roswell and Edwards
asked Rainer to produce objects that didn't

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:40.160
exist: a circular square, a color, and so
on.

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:45.040
But SCP-4051 wanted to know about his family
and when he would be able to go home before

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:47.040
he would try to manifest anything.

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:51.440
Roswell assured him that once the Foundation
had a solid grip on his ability, he would

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:53.040
be allowed to go home.

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:57.280
Questions about his family revealed that his
mother believed he was away visiting colleges.

00:04:57.280 --> 00:05:01.520
He demanded to speak to his mother before
any other experiments, and Roswell affirmed

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:06.000
that he'd ask the O5s for approval when the
experiment in question finished.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:10.960
Rainer agreed, and began the experiment, trying
to produce the impossible items.

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:15.760
What came out were cognitohazards, severely
damaging the mental state of anyone trying

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:16.880
to perceive them.

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:21.520
Half the research team instantly collapsed,
and security guards subdued Rainer to take

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:22.720
him back to his cell.

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:27.920
The testing chamber was cleaned and Dr. Edwards
wrote that the value of SCP-4051's anomaly

00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:31.120
was too great to let him sit in a box unused.

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:36.240
He called for a special pediatric therapist
and authorized further experiments on Rainer.

00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:40.800
But in his own containment cell, Rainer was
still knocked out after the test had gone

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:41.440
wrong.

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:46.240
The cameras watched on as he woke up and began
curling up and away from them toward the other

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:49.440
side of the room, then standing up a few minutes
later.

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:53.840
He had manifested many small pieces of body
armor and glued them to his body.

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:58.080
The guards were distracted with escorting
Roswell and Edwards from the testing chamber,

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:03.520
and didn't realize anything was wrong until
Rainer manifested a small bomb and blew his

00:06:03.520 --> 00:06:05.920
door open, leaving his cell.

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:11.040
Other security guards immediately turned and
responded, trying to subdue SCP-4051 with

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:12.480
nonlethal weapons.

00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:17.440
Eventually, a few were able to overpower and
incapacitate Rainer, and move him back to

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:18.240
his cell.

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:23.680
The day after the containment breach, Site-17's
director, Thomas Graham, sent out an open

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:27.040
letter to all staff assigned to SCP-4051.

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:31.760
Rainer had been moved to a more secure containment
unit, but everyone agrees that it would be

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:38.080
better in the long-run if SCP-4051 is working
for the Foundation rather than against it.

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:40.480
Especially with regards to amnestics.

00:06:40.480 --> 00:06:46.240
Sourcing Y909, a chemical used in amnestics,
was dangerous and expensive for the Foundation.

00:06:46.240 --> 00:06:50.720
But if Rainer's abilities could be harnessed
to produce amnestics easily, then he would

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:54.800
be all the more valuable to them as a friend
rather than foe.

00:06:54.800 --> 00:07:00.640
The Ethics Committee also require that SCP-4051
do so voluntarily for the Foundation, rather

00:07:00.640 --> 00:07:03.920
than being forced to produce amnestics against
his will.

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:09.920
To that, Doctor Edwards was promoted to SCP-4051's
Project Director on the basis that he would

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:14.880
try to ensure Rainer would be totally and
utterly loyal to the Foundation, using whatever

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:16.320
means necessary.

00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:21.520
He already set up a schedule using punishments
and rewards, along with regular checkups from

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:23.120
an on-site therapist.

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:25.360
The therapy sessions began on a good note.

00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:31.680
Dr. Yesenia, the therapist assigned to SCP-4051,
introduced herself politely, and Rainer seemed

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:32.960
to take a shine to her.

00:07:32.960 --> 00:07:36.640
They discussed his unique anomaly, and the
containment breach incident.

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:41.520
Yesenia was kind, and understood the psychological
toll containment had on people.

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:46.080
She asked why he wanted to escape, and he
explained he just wanted to see his family.

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:49.840
He was close with his mother, since his father
had walked out on them when Rainer was just

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:50.560
a boy.

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:54.080
They had been supporting each other since,
and he missed her a lot.

00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:57.680
That said, he explained he wasn't opposed
to living at the Foundation.

00:07:57.680 --> 00:08:02.240
They could help him actually understand his
powers, and he didn't mind being a part of

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:04.720
tests if he knew he was helping people.

00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:06.880
He just wanted to see his family again.

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:11.360
Yesenia's after-meeting note said that containment
efforts should be focused on assuring Rainer

00:08:11.360 --> 00:08:14.640
that the Foundation had his best interests
in mind.

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:17.920
The next set of experiments were a little
more abstract.

00:08:17.920 --> 00:08:22.720
Doctor Edwards alone was overseeing them,
and the first experiment included another

00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:24.800
individual, a D-class.

00:08:24.800 --> 00:08:29.360
The plan was to see if the D-class could also
pull things out of the portals, or if only

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:33.040
SCP-4051 was able to interact with his portals.

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:37.920
The D-class was scared of Rainer, but after
some urging by Dr. Edwards, he managed to

00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:42.480
touch the sides of the portals and reach in
and pull out a stone.

00:08:42.480 --> 00:08:47.280
Rainer was only anomalous in his ability to
manifest the portals, so Edwards' plan was

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:49.520
to cut out the middleman, and perform research&nbsp;

00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:53.120
on SCP-4051's brain to see&nbsp;
if they could successfully

00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:56.400
devise an artificial method of creating the
portals.

00:08:56.400 --> 00:09:01.200
The experiment after that was to see the bounds
and geographies of the pocket dimensions that

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:02.400
Rainer generated.

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:07.920
A GPS tracking chip was thrown into one of
the portals SCP-4051 made - specifically the

00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:10.320
portal leading to portraits of his mother.

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:13.680
The portal shut, then Rainer was asked to
recreate it.

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:17.200
The researchers checked to see if they could
still get a solid signal from the tracking

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:21.760
chip - and they did, albeit almost a thousand
kilometers away.

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:27.760
The results were filed away, but Edwards noticed
one thing - the portrait of SCP-4051's mother

00:09:27.760 --> 00:09:29.120
was slightly different.

00:09:29.120 --> 00:09:32.000
It seemed that he was forgetting what she
looked like.

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:36.800
The next therapy appointment with Doctor Yesenia
covered how Rainer felt about that experiment.

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:41.040
He was excited that they were actually performing
research about the anomaly that he wasn't

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:45.120
capable of just telling them, that they were
now finding out something interesting about

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:45.920
his powers.

00:09:45.920 --> 00:09:51.360
Yesenia asked if he had any requests for tests,
but he doubted that Edwards would listen to

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:52.800
anything he said.

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:57.040
The doctor seemed to dislike Rainer for some
reason he couldn't figure out, but he knew

00:09:57.040 --> 00:09:59.360
best on what to test and how.

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:04.320
Meanwhile, Edwards had come up with something
that could utilize SCP-4051's abilities in

00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:10.320
a useful way for the project of synthesizing
amnestics: Procedure 350-PROMETHEAN.

00:10:10.320 --> 00:10:15.200
The details of this clandestine project are
murky and secretive, but the goal was to see

00:10:15.200 --> 00:10:20.480
if they could use Rainer as a live method
of synthesizing Y909 through an experimental

00:10:20.480 --> 00:10:22.000
surgical procedure.

00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:26.880
Several contingencies were planned - if the
wormhole became too dangerous or Rainer tried

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:31.600
to resist, he'd be automatically injected
with paralytics and sent back to his cell.

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:34.080
The project wasn't immediately approved, though.

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:39.760
The Ethics Committee sent one of their most
skilled liaisons, Jeremiah Cimmerian, to conduct

00:10:39.760 --> 00:10:41.280
the approval process.

00:10:41.280 --> 00:10:43.440
He interviewed Dr. Edwards, ascertaining that&nbsp;

00:10:43.440 --> 00:10:45.840
the man was sane and able&nbsp;
to conduct the procedure.

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:50.640
That any unethical actions that were outside
the scope of the proposal would result in

00:10:50.640 --> 00:10:53.440
his removal from the team and disciplinary
action.

00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:59.200
Moreover, he revealed that he knew that Dr.
Roswell, SCP-4051's original researcher, was

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:04.000
Edwards' brother, and that he had been permanently
injured in the incident when Rainer was asked

00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:06.480
to manifest impossible objects.

00:11:06.480 --> 00:11:11.760
Edwards swore that he wouldn't take any needless
actions to cause intentional pain and suffering,

00:11:11.760 --> 00:11:15.840
and that everything that he would do would
be in the service of the Foundation's goals.

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:19.840
With that, Procedure 350-PROMETHEAN was approved.

00:11:19.840 --> 00:11:22.960
Meanwhile, Doctor Roswell's condition wasn't
improving.

00:11:22.960 --> 00:11:27.680
He had been put into an induced coma by medical
personnel due to his extensive exposure to

00:11:27.680 --> 00:11:29.200
the cognitohazards.

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:32.240
He wasn't expected to recover anytime soon.

00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:34.640
After the Ethics Committee approved the procedure,&nbsp;

00:11:34.640 --> 00:11:37.600
Doctor Edwards stopped&nbsp;
conducting usual experiments.

00:11:37.600 --> 00:11:41.120
The very next test involving SCP-4051 was&nbsp;

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:44.480
the first implementation of&nbsp;
Procedure 350-PROMETHEAN,

00:11:44.480 --> 00:11:45.600
but it failed.

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:50.080
Rainer broke the restraints on the chair during
the painful procedure, and Edwards considered

00:11:50.080 --> 00:11:54.720
tranquilizing him but decided against it:
"we need it awake" He said.

00:11:54.720 --> 00:11:58.960
The next therapy session, though, Rainer didn't
so much as mention the procedure.

00:11:58.960 --> 00:12:03.040
Instead, he greeted Doctor Yesenia, explaining
that he wasn't doing so well.

00:12:03.040 --> 00:12:07.360
He had talked back to a guard and they had
taken his desk away as punishment, and he

00:12:07.360 --> 00:12:08.960
felt like it was his own fault.

00:12:08.960 --> 00:12:13.440
Doctor Yesenia was worried and offered to
see if she could get the desk back, but he

00:12:13.440 --> 00:12:16.800
declined the offer, saying he'd just try to
be better.

00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:21.760
After the session, Yesenia felt annoyed - not
by Rainer, but by Edwards.

00:12:21.760 --> 00:12:26.160
He had been saying that the subject was getting
resentful and rude, but Rainer still seemed

00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:28.160
like a sweet, helpful child.

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:32.960
The next time Procedure 350-PROMETHEAN was
enacted, it was the first time Edwards actually

00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:35.120
managed to successfully complete it.

00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:40.400
SCP-4051 was actually being compliant with
the procedure, making the job a lot easier

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:41.680
for the surgical staff.

00:12:41.680 --> 00:12:44.960
The results and details of it, however, were
still unclear.

00:12:44.960 --> 00:12:49.040
In the therapy session after that, Rainer
told Doctor Yesenia that he had been having

00:12:49.040 --> 00:12:51.360
terrible, terrible dreams every night.

00:12:51.360 --> 00:12:53.760
Nightmares that stopped him from sleeping.

00:12:53.760 --> 00:12:57.920
He worried that people would treat him like
a freak - not because of his anomaly, but

00:12:57.920 --> 00:13:00.160
because of what had happened with his father.

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:02.720
Doctor Yesenia encouraged him to tell her.

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:07.120
She already knew, but felt it would be good
if he let it out - and he shared his memories

00:13:07.120 --> 00:13:12.000
of how his father had locked him in a closet
and abused him, burning him with bleach.

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:16.400
That's why he'd been upset when asked to take
a bottle of bleach in the first test.

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:21.440
His nightmares were about not being able to
escape something that was coming toward him.

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:24.400
And that his father could still be out there.

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:28.720
But Yesenia admitted to him that while she
shouldn't be telling him, his father had been

00:13:28.720 --> 00:13:30.080
found by the Foundation.

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:33.840
He was serving a life sentence in an Arkansas
prison for murder.

00:13:33.840 --> 00:13:37.360
Rainer grew quiet for a moment before changing
the subject.

00:13:37.360 --> 00:13:42.320
Yesenia's observations were optimistic, and
she believed his mental health was improving

00:13:42.320 --> 00:13:46.400
and that he was now fitting into his role
at the Foundation, though she wondered how

00:13:46.400 --> 00:13:48.560
Edwards' experiments with him were going.

00:13:48.560 --> 00:13:51.440
The next implementation of&nbsp;
Procedure 350-PROMETHEAN&nbsp;

00:13:51.440 --> 00:13:52.400
went poorly.

00:13:52.400 --> 00:13:57.280
Edwards wrote in his diary angrily afterwards,
that Rainer didn't even remember Roswell or

00:13:57.280 --> 00:13:58.720
recognize his name.

00:13:58.720 --> 00:14:03.280
How he was angry that he was assigned to the
anomaly that had nearly killed his brother.

00:14:03.280 --> 00:14:07.040
He'd had an outburst during the experiment
and it was shut down early.

00:14:07.040 --> 00:14:10.320
But only a week after, another attempt was
made.

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:15.040
While the procedure was being done, Rainer
asked about Roswell, but was cut off.

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:19.840
The research team knew that if he was told
what he had done to Doctor Roswell, his mental

00:14:19.840 --> 00:14:22.640
health would crater and negatively affect
the project.

00:14:22.640 --> 00:14:27.600
In spite of that, the procedure was a success,
and Edwards' took credit for the whole thing.

00:14:27.600 --> 00:14:34.000
They were getting closer to being able to
completely make use of SCP-4051's anomaly.

00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:38.800
In his next therapy session, Rainer recounted
how he liked being out and about in nature,

00:14:38.800 --> 00:14:42.160
and how the containment cell had become a
suffocating prison.

00:14:42.160 --> 00:14:46.560
Yesenia suggested she might be able to swing
a treadmill in his room to keep him active

00:14:46.560 --> 00:14:50.480
if she bothered her superiors, but he didn't
want her to get in trouble.

00:14:50.480 --> 00:14:55.040
He seemed worried and upset - he voiced that
he didn't think these experiments were helping

00:14:55.040 --> 00:14:57.920
people anymore, that he was being a burden.

00:14:57.920 --> 00:15:03.200
Yesenia had an idea - she could ask the Director
to allow Rainer to help out around the site,

00:15:03.200 --> 00:15:05.920
fixing little things and helping clean things
up.

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:10.560
It wasn't much, but it would allow him some
activity and boost his morale about helping

00:15:10.560 --> 00:15:13.200
people all while making use of his anomaly.

00:15:13.200 --> 00:15:17.840
Rainer was excited - he loved the idea, and
had been scared of being stuck in his cell

00:15:17.840 --> 00:15:18.800
uselessly.

00:15:18.800 --> 00:15:24.240
After the session, Yesenia reflected that
it seemed cruel to manipulate SCP-4051 into

00:15:24.240 --> 00:15:28.720
wanting to help the Foundation when he so
obviously already wants to help.

00:15:28.720 --> 00:15:33.520
And just like she said, it didn't take long
for the Director to authorize a security clearance

00:15:33.520 --> 00:15:39.200
for SCP-4051, just enough to be outside of
his cell when accompanied, to help with site

00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:40.000
maintenance.

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:44.720
While Rainer was off fixing things around
the site, Yesenia decided to do some digging,

00:15:44.720 --> 00:15:48.880
and asked for information about the experiments
Edwards was conducting, but didn't have a

00:15:48.880 --> 00:15:50.160
high enough clearance.

00:15:50.160 --> 00:15:55.920
Meanwhile, Edwards had come up with a prototype
for a machine that can mimic SCP-4051's abilities.

00:15:55.920 --> 00:16:01.760
A few weeks after it was approved, Site-17
had a minor containment breach and a few hostile

00:16:01.760 --> 00:16:04.080
anomalies overran armed personnel.

00:16:04.080 --> 00:16:08.560
Rainer was present at the time and used his
wormholes to terminate the anomalies before

00:16:08.560 --> 00:16:10.400
containment was reestablished.

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:15.920
Even though he saved lives, Yesenia was forced
to reprimand him for using his powers without

00:16:15.920 --> 00:16:20.000
authorization, and he was banned from any
maintenance for two months.

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:25.200
Several months later, the machine to mimic
Rainer's powers, 350-JANUS, isn't working

00:16:25.200 --> 00:16:28.080
correctly and keeps producing the wrong object.

00:16:28.080 --> 00:16:33.600
Yesenia keeps requesting information on Edwards'
experiments, but is denied every time, even

00:16:33.600 --> 00:16:36.880
when she asks the Ethics Committee for a review
on the project.

00:16:36.880 --> 00:16:40.880
The machine worked, but only once, breaking
right after.

00:16:40.880 --> 00:16:47.120
SCP-4051's story is a strange one - it involved
an MTF mission sent into a dangerous area

00:16:47.120 --> 00:16:50.400
to contain an object, with Rainer sent along
with them.

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:55.360
The full mission log has yet to be declassified,
and maybe we'll cover it in a future video.

00:16:55.360 --> 00:16:59.280
But for now, let's just say something went
wrong during that mission.

00:16:59.280 --> 00:17:05.360
The Foundation discovered something new and
dangerous about SCP-4051's powers, and a closer

00:17:05.360 --> 00:17:07.280
eye fell upon the project.

00:17:07.280 --> 00:17:13.040
The Ethics Committee reevaluated what had
gone on with SCP-4051, and the Site Director

00:17:13.040 --> 00:17:15.760
surrendered information -&nbsp;
that Edwards' experiments&nbsp;

00:17:15.760 --> 00:17:18.320
hadn't been all in the name of science.

00:17:18.320 --> 00:17:23.760
That he might have been needlessly cruel and
violent to an innocent anomaly, just because

00:17:23.760 --> 00:17:27.360
he wanted revenge for the accidental mutilation
of his brother.

00:17:27.360 --> 00:17:32.880
After taking a closer look, the Ethics Committee
came to the decision that SCP-4051 needed

00:17:32.880 --> 00:17:34.240
to be re-thought.

00:17:34.240 --> 00:17:38.880
Large portions of the document were redacted
and classified, and they tried to bury the

00:17:38.880 --> 00:17:39.760
project.

00:17:39.760 --> 00:17:45.680
SCP-4051's powers were too dangerous to allow
about the site - his permissions were revoked,

00:17:45.680 --> 00:17:49.760
and he was placed into permanent containment
in a more specialized cell.

00:17:49.760 --> 00:17:52.640
The researchers of the Foundation need oversight.

00:17:52.640 --> 00:17:58.240
Otherwise, you get incidents like SCP-4051,
where a vengeful doctor subjected an otherwise

00:17:58.240 --> 00:18:04.320
innocent being to brutal surgical experiments
and manipulation under the guise of research.

00:18:04.320 --> 00:18:06.560
It goes to show that the Foundation isn't&nbsp;

00:18:06.560 --> 00:18:09.440
always the good guy - in&nbsp;
fact, from the perspective

00:18:09.440 --> 00:18:13.760
of the anomalies, the Foundation can be pretty
damn evil.

00:18:13.760 --> 00:18:19.760
Now go check out “SCP-4999 - Someone to
Watch Over Us Tale” and “SCP-999 - The

00:18:19.760 --> 00:18:24.560
Tickle Monster” for more anomalies of the
friendly nature from SCP Explained!

